# The resume lives at /resume-cifz9eqb (readable, but with enough entropy
# in the suffix that it can't be enumerated or guessed — see CLAUDE.md).
# A bare /resume must not exist or redirect anywhere. To keep the real path
# out of search results anyway, every response for it carries X-Robots-Tag —
# this is the only way to mark the PDF noindex, since a PDF can't carry a
# <meta> tag. The HTML page also repeats this via a <meta name="robots">
# tag in src/pages/resume-cifz9eqb.astro.
#
# NOTE: the @astrojs/cloudflare adapter injects its own immutable
# Cache-Control block for /_astro/* at the top of this file during
# `astro build` (see astro:build:done in @astrojs/cloudflare) — it prepends
# rather than overwrites, so this file's own rules below are preserved as-is
# on every build. Don't reorder this file expecting it to stay put.
/resume-cifz9eqb
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, noai, noimageai

/resume-cifz9eqb.pdf
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, noai, noimageai
